 ## Overview
-SXMPVO is an algorithm for determining the visibility ordering of cells in nonconvex unstructured meshes for volume rendering [S2, S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem that the standard Maximal Polyhedra Visibility Ordering (MPVO) method fails for nonconvex meshes because it ignores ordering relations along viewing rays that cross empty space ("ray-gaps") between non-adjacent cells [S2, unofficial]. SXMPVO achieves "image-space correctness" by combining MPVO's face-based partial ordering with scan-conversion of exterior faces into an A-Buffer to resolve these ray-gaps [S2, S3, unofficial]. Unlike object-precision methods like XMPVO, SXMPVO uses image-precision ray shooting, making it faster and simpler to implement while guaranteeing correct sorting for acyclic meshes [S2, S3, unofficial].
+SXMPVO is an image-space visibility ordering algorithm for cell projection volume rendering of unstructured data [S2, S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem that the standard Maximal Polyhedra Visibility Ordering (MPVO) method fails for nonconvex meshes because it ignores ordering relations along viewing rays that cross empty space ("ray-gaps") between non-adjacent cells [S2, unofficial]. SXMPVO achieves "image-space correctness" by combining MPVO's face-based partial ordering with scan-conversion of exterior faces into an A-Buffer to resolve these ray-gaps [S2, S3, unofficial]. Unlike object-precision methods like XMPVO, SXMPVO uses image-precision ray shooting, making it faster and simpler to implement while guaranteeing correct sorting for acyclic meshes [S2, S3, unofficial].
 
